  "body": "This should be mostly similar to the Anolis version, minus the following differences:\n- Typo fix: \"create a notification\" steps, step 5, +\"option's\".\n- Typo fix: \"create a notification\" steps, step 8, s/notifications's/notification's/.\n- Typo fix: ...when invoked, must return these steps  s/return/run/.\n\nThere are two problems I ran in to.\n\n(1) IDL generation doesn't like the \"any\" data type. It doesn't insert a space between the property's type and name, e.g. \"readonly attribute anydata;\" and \"anydata = null;\".\n(2) IDL generation fails on use of the \"required\" keyword in a dictionary. According to WebIRL, [this is allowed](http://heycam.github.io/webidl/#required-dictionary-member).\n\nFATAL ERROR: IDL SYNTAX ERROR LINE: 20 - skipped: \"required Notification notification\"\n",
